Built-Using: ${misc:Built-Using}
Description: doctor for Linux servers: finds problems and gives the fix
 nabd checks a Linux machine in about a second: disk space and inodes,
 memory, CPU, failed services, kernel log errors, time sync, pending
 reboots, package state, network and DNS, open ports, SSH settings, TLS
 certificates, processes and accounts. For each problem it explains the
 cause in plain words and prints the command that fixes it.
 .
 "nabd why" explores one question in depth (disk, slow, memory, service,
 port, dns, boot). "nabd changes" shows a timeline of recent changes, and
 "nabd snapshot" with "nabd diff" finds drift such as new admin users,
 SUID files or open ports.
 .
 nabd only reads: it never changes the system. Its output is text, JSON,
 Markdown, Nagios plugin output or Prometheus metrics.
